1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,060
How the British Empire tried to solve a problem and accidentally made it much worse.

2
00:00:04,060 --> 00:00:05,840
Explained like you are five.

3
00:00:05,840 --> 00:00:08,560
Step one, it is 1800 colonial India.

4
00:00:08,560 --> 00:00:11,720
The British are running the country and Delhi has a problem.

5
00:00:11,720 --> 00:00:12,560
Cobras.

6
00:00:12,560 --> 00:00:14,280
Venomous cobras everywhere.

7
00:00:14,280 --> 00:00:17,140
In the streets, in the homes, killing people.

8
00:00:17,140 --> 00:00:19,860
The British colonial government decides to fix this.

9
00:00:19,860 --> 00:00:20,820
Their solution?

10
00:00:20,820 --> 00:00:23,320
Pay people money for every dead cobra they bring in.

11
00:00:23,320 --> 00:00:26,560
Simple, logical, efficient, kill a cobra.

12
00:00:26,560 --> 00:00:28,520
Get paid, fewer cobras.

13
00:00:28,520 --> 00:00:29,640
Problem solved.

14
00:00:29,720 --> 00:00:31,640
Except the problem is not solved.

15
00:00:31,640 --> 00:00:35,240
The problem is about to get significantly worse because the British forgot one thing

16
00:00:35,240 --> 00:00:36,640
about human beings.

17
00:00:36,640 --> 00:00:40,560
Give people a financial incentive, and they will find a way to maximize it.

18
00:00:40,560 --> 00:00:42,360
Whether you intended that or not.

19
00:00:42,360 --> 00:00:43,360
Step two.

20
00:00:43,360 --> 00:00:44,360
The bounty works at first.

21
00:00:44,360 --> 00:00:47,640
People go out, hunt cobras, bring in dead snakes, collect money.

22
00:00:47,640 --> 00:00:51,200
The government is pleased, but then something unexpected happens.

23
00:00:51,200 --> 00:00:53,360
Entrepreneurial Indians realize something.

24
00:00:53,360 --> 00:00:55,480
You do not have to hunt cobras in the wild.

25
00:00:55,480 --> 00:00:56,560
You can breed them.

26
00:00:56,560 --> 00:00:57,560
At home.

27
00:00:57,560 --> 00:00:58,560
In boxes.

28
00:00:58,560 --> 00:01:00,240
It costs almost nothing to keep.

29
00:01:00,240 --> 00:01:01,440
It eats very little.

30
00:01:01,440 --> 00:01:03,640
It produces eggs constantly.

31
00:01:03,640 --> 00:01:06,380
And every single one of those eggs hatches into a bounty.

32
00:01:06,380 --> 00:01:10,200
So people start cobra farms, hundreds of cobras, thousands of cobras.

33
00:01:10,200 --> 00:01:14,000
All bred specifically to be killed and exchanged for British money.

34
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:15,000
Step three.

35
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:17,400
The government notices the bounty payments are going up.

36
00:01:17,400 --> 00:01:18,400
Way up.

37
00:01:18,400 --> 00:01:21,800
Far more cobras are being turned in than could possibly exist in Delhi.

38
00:01:21,800 --> 00:01:22,800
They investigate.

39
00:01:22,800 --> 00:01:23,800
They find the cobra farms.

40
00:01:23,800 --> 00:01:25,620
They realize what has happened.

41
00:01:25,620 --> 00:01:27,040
So they do the sensible thing.

42
00:01:27,040 --> 00:01:29,180
They cancel the bounty program.

43
00:01:29,180 --> 00:01:30,920
No more payments for dead cobras.

44
00:01:30,920 --> 00:01:32,840
The cobra farms are now worthless.

45
00:01:32,840 --> 00:01:35,280
You have a shed full of cobras that earn you nothing.

46
00:01:35,280 --> 00:01:37,560
So the farmers do the only logical thing.

47
00:01:37,560 --> 00:01:39,920
They release all the cobras.

48
00:01:39,920 --> 00:01:42,360
Thousands of captive bred cobras.

49
00:01:42,360 --> 00:01:44,000
Released into the streets of Delhi.

50
00:01:44,000 --> 00:01:48,080
The cobra population is now significantly larger than when they started.

51
00:01:48,080 --> 00:01:49,080
Step four.

52
00:01:49,080 --> 00:01:52,380
The British colonial government tried to reduce the cobra population.

53
00:01:52,380 --> 00:01:55,400
Their solution created a cobra farming industry.

54
00:01:55,400 --> 00:01:58,040
Designing the solution released thousands of new cobras.

55
00:01:58,040 --> 00:02:01,780
The problem they tried to fix, now worse than before they tried to fix it.

56
00:02:01,780 --> 00:02:03,480
This is the cobra effect.

57
00:02:03,480 --> 00:02:07,320
When a solution to a problem creates a bigger version of the same problem.

58
00:02:07,320 --> 00:02:11,080
It happens because the people designing the solution think about the goal.

59
00:02:11,080 --> 00:02:13,800
But not about how people will respond to the incentive.

60
00:02:13,800 --> 00:02:16,520
And people always respond to the incentive.

61
00:02:16,520 --> 00:02:18,480
Not the goal.

62
00:02:18,480 --> 00:02:19,480
Step five.

63
00:02:19,480 --> 00:02:23,000
The cobra effect is everywhere once you know what to look for.

64
00:02:23,000 --> 00:02:25,160
Vietnam under French colonial rule.

65
00:02:25,160 --> 00:02:26,160
Same problem.

66
00:02:26,160 --> 00:02:27,160
Same solution.

67
00:02:27,160 --> 00:02:28,160
Same result.

68
00:02:28,160 --> 00:02:29,420
The French paid a bounty on rat tails.

69
00:02:29,420 --> 00:02:30,600
People started rat farms.

70
00:02:30,600 --> 00:02:33,720
When the bounty was canceled, rats released.

71
00:02:33,720 --> 00:02:35,300
More rats than before.

72
00:02:35,300 --> 00:02:39,120
In 1990s America, schools were measured by test scores.

73
00:02:39,120 --> 00:02:41,700
So teachers started teaching only to the test.

74
00:02:41,700 --> 00:02:42,960
Test scores went up.

75
00:02:42,960 --> 00:02:44,640
Actual learning went down.

76
00:02:44,640 --> 00:02:49,040
In the 2000s, banks were rewarded for giving out as many mortgages as possible.

77
00:02:49,040 --> 00:02:55,240
So they gave mortgages to anyone, good or bad, and created the 2008 financial crisis.

78
00:02:55,240 --> 00:02:56,440
Step six.

79
00:02:56,440 --> 00:03:00,120
The cobra effect has a name now because of an economist called Horst Seibert.

80
00:03:00,120 --> 00:03:03,320
He wrote about it in 2001, but the pattern is ancient.

81
00:03:03,320 --> 00:03:08,060
Every time a government or a company or a person creates an incentive, someone somewhere

82
00:03:08,060 --> 00:03:11,480
will find the most efficient way to satisfy the incentive.

83
00:03:11,480 --> 00:03:13,240
Not the spirit of the incentive.

84
00:03:13,240 --> 00:03:14,240
The lettering.

85
00:03:14,240 --> 00:03:17,600
The gap between what you measure and what you actually want.

86
00:03:17,600 --> 00:03:20,360
That gap is where the cobra farms are built.

87
00:03:20,360 --> 00:03:24,680
The British Empire had the most powerful government on earth and they made the cobra problem worse

88
00:03:24,680 --> 00:03:26,080
by trying to fix it.

89
00:03:26,080 --> 00:03:31,240
So next time someone offers you a simple solution to a complicated problem, ask yourself, what

90
00:03:31,240 --> 00:03:32,680
are the cobra farms?

91
00:03:32,680 --> 00:03:35,320
